ubMed:11573934, PubMed:12084581, PubMed:21733844, PubMed:23382902, PubMed:30420639). Could also be permeable to urea (PubMed:12084581). Among aquaglyceroporins, it exhibits a unique pH-gated glycerol transport activity, being more active at acidic pH. It most likely plays a central role in the efflux of glycerol formed during triglyceride hydrolysis in adipocytes and in glycerol uptake by enterocytes, as both processes occur and are stimulated at acidic pH (PubMed:11573934, PubMed:23382902, PubMed:30420639)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "glycerol(in) = glycerol(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29675"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:17754"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12084581"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21733844"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23382902"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "H2O(in) = H2O(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29667"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11573934"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12084581"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21733844"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23382902"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "urea(in) = urea(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:32799"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:16199"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12084581"}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"